# This monorepo tracks CODE only. Data is wired via symlinks (see
# shared/snrnaseq_de/ and ~/Github/DATA_LAYOUT.md). Each subdir also carries its
# own .gitignore (inherited from its source repo), which governs that subtree.

# snRNA-seq DE interface — symlinked data, never committed
shared/snrnaseq_de/*.csv
shared/snrnaseq_de/*.tsv
# The composition betas are the exception: the original was never staged down
# from the cluster, so the copy here was regenerated by re-running the repo's own
# composition scripts (PROVENANCE.md records the checks). It is 17 KB and the
# whole of genetics/, S6 and S8 need it, so it is tracked rather than symlinked.
shared/snrnaseq_de/nicole_scz_snrnaseq_betas/*
!shared/snrnaseq_de/nicole_scz_snrnaseq_betas/final_results_crumblr_7_cohorts.csv
!shared/snrnaseq_de/nicole_scz_snrnaseq_betas/PROVENANCE.md

# cross-component data seams (symlinks -> originals/shared; see DATA_FLOW.md)
transcriptomic/data/*.csv
spatial/output/
spatial/data/nicole_scz_snrnaseq_betas
genetics/data/gwas/*.csv
histology/coordinates

# generic safety net
**/data/*.h5ad
**/*.rds
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Fig. 4 panels f/g raw patch-seq data: NWB recordings are large binaries kept
# out of git; the SWC reconstructions are small text and are committed.
# See genetics/data/patchseq/README.md
genetics/data/patchseq/nwb/*.nwb

# Superseded panel-K exploration (5.7 MB). Kept on disk as a methods-provenance
# record of the edgeR-vs-mixed-model comparison and the old exemplar-selection
# rule, but its tables predate the canonical April+PMI DE — one of them flips
# PVALB across p = 0.05. Ignored so `git add -A` cannot sweep it into the repo.
transcriptomic/scratch_panelK/

# ---- Sst depletion-strata (S8) pipeline, transcriptomic/scripts/fig5/ ----
# Cluster exports feeding steps 01-04 (1.6 GB of parquet/h5ad). Only the manifests
# and the tiny summary tables are tracked; shared/snrnaseq_de/EXPORT_SPEC_*.md
# says how to regenerate them on the cluster.
transcriptomic/data/stratum_pseudobulks_export/*
!transcriptomic/data/stratum_pseudobulks_export/MANIFEST.md
!transcriptomic/data/stratum_pseudobulks_export/_export_summary.csv
!transcriptomic/data/stratum_pseudobulks_export/_marker_check.csv
transcriptomic/data/stratum_sst_cells_export/*
!transcriptomic/data/stratum_sst_cells_export/MANIFEST_sst_cells.md
!transcriptomic/data/stratum_sst_cells_export/_sst_reconciliation.csv
# Results: track the canonical tables the fig5 README lists (what 08_figure5.R and
# 09_verify.R read), not the per-cohort tables (24-42 MB), donor-stratum parquets,
# msigdb cache, exploratory PNGs, or the reserve (Jens / SEA-AD A9 / cell-subsample)
# analyses, all regenerable from the numbered scripts.
transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/*
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/strata_definition.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/xenium_stratum_concordance.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/xenium_sst_baseline_controls.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/sst_baseline_vs_depletion.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/suppl_table_strata_gsea_annotated.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/pseudobulk/
transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/pseudobulk/*
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/pseudobulk/stratum_meta_de.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/pseudobulk/gsea_all_signatures.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/pseudobulk/stratum_gene_signatures.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/pseudobulk/interaction_meta.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/pseudobulk/interaction_gsea.csv
!transcriptomic/results/sst_strata_gsea/pseudobulk/module_score_tests.csv

# ---- Parked 8th cohort (GSE158516): code + README only ----
reserve/gse158516/data/
reserve/gse158516/output/

# ---- Reading material and internal notes: not part of the paper ----
background/

# R side-effect file from non-interactive ggsave sessions
Rplots.pdf

# Hand-editing SVGs of the main figures: the patch-seq traces make Figure 4's
# ~25 MB. PNG + PDF are the deliverables.
manuscript/figures/main/*.svg

# ---- Per-cell metadata dumps: never in the repo ----
# `write.csv(seu@meta.data, ...)` with no column selection emits one row per cell
# and every column the upstream object happened to carry. That is 2.8 GB across
# these files, to serve six columns anything downstream actually reads -- and for
# the Batiuk object it also emitted the donating brain banks' clinical records
# (KNOWN_ISSUES issue 24). The small derived inputs beside them are committed;
# these are not. Regenerate on the cluster.
snrnaseq/Compositional_sensitivity_analysis/Files/*_NoSST_DEgenes.csv
!snrnaseq/Compositional_sensitivity_analysis/Files/7_cohorts_metadata_NoSST_DEgenes_names.csv
snrnaseq/Final_figures/Data/xenium_metadata.csv

# Zenodo downloads cached by transcriptomic/scripts/00b_figure_inputs_from_zenodo.py
transcriptomic/data/.zenodo_cache/

# Per-donor genotype-derived analysis — deliberately NOT published (2026-09-16).
# reserve/genotype/data/donor_table.csv carries, per identifiable donor, 10 genetic
# ancestry PCs, a superpopulation label, three polygenic risk scores and AD
# neuropathology (Braak/CERAD). That is derived genotype data, a different
# sensitivity class from the demographic sheet cleared in KNOWN_ISSUES issue 6, and
# the upstream genotypes arrive under NDA/Synapse/PsychAD agreements that restrict
# redistribution of individual-level derived data. The analysis is also reserve/ —
# not in the paper — so publishing it carries the risk with none of the benefit.
# Ignored so it cannot be committed by accident. Do not un-ignore without a DUA
# check and explicit PI sign-off on THIS content.
reserve/genotype/

# Large DE tables, removed from Git LFS 2026-09-16 — published on Zenodo instead
# (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22801230). See the root README, section "Published data".
snrnaseq/snRNAseq_DE/Files/DE_genes_all_cohorts_subclass.csv
snrnaseq/snRNAseq_DE/Supertypes/Files/DE_all_cohorts_meta_supertype.csv
snrnaseq/snRNAseq_DE/Supertypes/Files/DE_meta_results_supertype.csv
snrnaseq/snRNAseq_DE/Supertypes/Files/DE_results_cohorts_supertype.csv
